```

Offline, so `validate_program` / `analyze_schedule` / `visualize_schedule` could not be called — run them live to publish the timeline. Checked by hand against the rules: all `stepId`s unique; every track's steps chained with `afterStep` and non-overlapping; every task (`lane`, `blocks`, `coach`) has a matching `resourceConstraint`; `instances: "all"` only references the replicated `sprint` step; no `replicates` on any `"each"`-style step. With the planning defaults the crew clears the deck at **exactly 150 minutes** (brief 0–5, warm-up 5–25, whiteboard 25–30, kick 30–50, mains 50–100, sprints 100–130, cooldown 130–140, debrief 140–150), and because lane 3's plan already equals its 50-minute maximum, overruns in lanes 1 and 2 do not push past the pool-time cap — the binding constraint is the single set of blocks, not the lanes.
